Z||000002||BBBAD GT||04-28-2000||11:58 AM||||Here is the info that was emailed to me:<P><BR>You're Invited to Attend the 6th Annual Gateway Fiero Club Car Show.<BR>Saturday, April 29, 2000 at The Museum of Transportation - 3015 Barrett <BR>Station Road  - St. Louis, MO  63122<BR>10am-3:30pm<P>Schedule<BR>Friday, April 28 after 4 pm  check into hotel<BR>6-8pm   meet in the bar area of the hotel and get registration packet<BR>8pm     meet other Fiero owners in the bar area of the hotel and go next <BR>door to Dave & Buster's for a night of funSaturday<P>April 29<BR>Early   get up and get started cleaning Fiero<BR>9am     meet in the parking lot of the hotel to convoy to the car show<BR>9-10am  arrive at the Museum of Transportation<BR>Noon    voting starts<BR>2:30pm  voting ends<BR>3:30pm  car show ends<BR>4pm     banquet ends<P>Contact Number's<BR>Day of Show)Kim Gerecke 314-517-7147<BR>            Karen Thorn 314-952-2661<P>Where are we spending the night?<BR>We have rooms blocked at the:<BR>Doubletree Club Hotel Riverport13735 Riverport Drive, Maryland Heights, MO  <BR>63043<BR>314-298-3400<BR>Rooms are $59/night (+tax).  Mention the Fiero Club to get this rate.  You <BR>must make your reservation by April 14, to guarantee availability and this <BR>rate.<BR>The hotel offers a restaurant, bar, shuttle service within 5 miles and a hot <BR>tub.<BR>The hotel is located just south of I-70 off Earth City Expressway - which is <BR>just west of I-270.  It's right next door to Dave & Buster's and within a <BR>half mile of the Riverport Amphitheater.  It is within shuttle distance of <BR>the Riverport Casino Center and the Station Casino - St. Charles, Main <BR>Street in St. Charles as well as several shops and restaurants.<P>Questions?  Need More Info?contact us at:  StLFieros@aol.com<BR>Classes for the Car Show<BR>A.  Stock Coupe - 4 cyl.<BR>B.  Stock Coupe - 6 cyl.<BR>C.  Stock Formula<BR>D.  Stock GT<BR>E.  Custom GT<BR>F.  Custom Coupe/Formula<BR>G.  Modified<BR>H.  Rebody<BR>I.  Daily Driver<BR>We will also be voting on Best of Show.<BR>The Museum of Transportation charges a small admission fee to<BR>non-participnts, which allows people to see a piece of history and our <BR>awesome car show.  For those of you showing your Fiero, you will get free <BR>access to this fabulous museum. BanquetImmediately Following Car Show at The <BR>Museum of Transportation BBQ Buffet Includes:<BR>2 meats potato salad slaw baked beans dessert iced tea, coffee drink ticket <BR>for 1 bottled beverage<BR>cost is $10/person Registration Fees<BR>$20 Registrations postmarked by April 14<BR>$25 Registrations day of show and postmarked after April 14<BR>$10 per person - Banquet<BR>$2  per extra dash plaque<BR>All registrations must be postmarked by April 14, 2000.<BR>Make checks payable to our club Treasurer: Kim Gerecke475 Bellingham <BR>Court,St. Charles, MO  63304<BR>_________________________________||||reg||1
